,title,link,text,language,family
0,Yanyuwa people - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yanyuwa_people,"The Yanyuwa people, also spelt Yanuwa, Yanyula and other variations, are an Aboriginal Australian people of the Northern Territory who live in the coastal region inclusive of and opposite to the Sir Edward Pellew Group of Islands in the southern Gulf of Carpentaria.",Yanyuwa,Australian
1,Yanyuwa language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yanyuwa_language,"Yanyuwa, like many other Australian Aboriginal languages, is a highly agglutinative language with ergative-absolutive alignment, whose grammar is pervaded by a set of 16 noun classes whose agreements are complicated and numerous. Yanyuwa is a critically endangered language.",Yanyuwa,Australian
2,Music - Singing the knowledge - Yanyuwa kujika - Lynne Kelly,https://www.lynnekelly.com.au/?page_id=559,"A wonderful collaboration between the Yanyuwa people and Monash University is online and enables us to glimpse the singing tracks of their culture. The Yanyuwa live 0n the Gulf Carpentaria in Northern Australia. Animations of the songs can be seen at the Monash Country Lines Archive. As described in his 2010 book, Singing Saltwater Country John Bradley has ...",Yanyuwa,Australian
3,"Gulf country songbook : Yanyuwa, Marra, Garrwa and Gudanji songs ...",https://catalogue.nla.gov.au/catalog/7011362,"The songs, stories and images in this book, and the accompanying CD and DVD, contain traditional knowledge of the Yanyuwa, Marra, Garrwa and Gudanji peoples, published with the consent of senior knowledge custodians.",Yanyuwa,Australian
4,Acclaimed Yanyuwa and Wardaman singer-songwriter Shellie Morris Music ...,https://www.facebook.com/AWMAAwards/videos/acclaimed-yanyuwa-and-wardaman-singer-songwriter-shellie-morris-music-has-dedica/1600293065362107/,"Acclaimed Yanyuwa and Wardaman singer-songwriter Shellie Morris Music has dedicated more than 25 years to using music as a tool for healing, language preservation and cultural storytelling. She is a multi- award-winning artist who has performed in more than 20 First Languages across Australia, and is widely recognised for her work supporting Indigenous communities and cultural continuity ...",Yanyuwa,Australian
5,Yanyuwa - ictv.com.au,https://ictv.com.au/languages/196-yanyuwa,ICTV Play language videos for Yanyuwa. Download our app on your phone! Stream all your favourite content on the go.,Yanyuwa,Australian
6,Songs From The Gulf Country — Wunungu Awara,https://www.wununguawara.org/animations/gulfsongs,"In recent times the Yanyuwa community have used animation to preserve knowledge that people do not want to lose. The Songs from the Gulf Country is a collection of five Yanyuwa songs that have ""passed the test"" and are still sung to this day.",Yanyuwa,Australian
7,Our Story — Wunungu Awara,https://www.wununguawara.org/ourstory,"John also witnessed first hand the lack of understanding displayed by non-Aboriginal colleagues towards Aboriginal history and culture in Australia. As a result he began a career in research and academia, working with the Yanyuwa people, learning their language, stories and songs.",Yanyuwa,Australian
8,Shellie Morris,https://shelliemorris.com/,"Multi-Award Winning Yanyuwa & Wardaman Singer/Songwriter. Dr. Shellie Morris AO has dedicated 25 years to using music as a healing tool. She emphasises the significance of individual voices and was honoured with the Officer of the Order of Australia for her contributions to the performing arts, Indigenous community, and not-for-profit ...",Yanyuwa,Australian
9,"Singing the land, singing the family: Song, place and spirituality ...",https://research.monash.edu/en/publications/singing-the-land-singing-the-family-song-place-and-spirituality-a,"Yanyuwa people and culture are located, before a discussion of the interrelationship of Yanyuwa concepts about music, place and spirituality through lived engagement and constant negotiation with memory and country.",Yanyuwa,Australian
